  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="n08e74995abb9464aa6e0566a52d52212b44">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An attack (noun) is the use of an exploit(s) by an adversary to take advantage of a weakness(s) with the intent of achieving a negative technical impact(s).

Source: https://capec.mitre.org/about/glossary.html#Attack

From the bove definition, "the use of an exploit(s)" is means, "an adversary" is attacker, and "to take advantage of... with the intent of achieving a negative technical impact(s)" is consequence.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"/>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://ffrdc.ebiquity.umbc.edu/ns/ontology/#Attack"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget>An attack (noun) is the use of an exploit(s) by an adversary to take advantage of a weakness(s) with the intent of achieving a negative technical impact(s).

Source: https://capec.mitre.org/about/glossary.html#Attack

From the bove definition, "the use of an exploit(s)" is means, "an adversary" is attacker, and "negative technical impact(s)" is consequence.</owl:annotatedTarget>
  </rdf:Description>
